Tested against the brief in the appendix of the feedback report: it
reports the five bare `unsourced:` lines and every entry without an
ID. A corrected copy, split into one brief per commit, passes, as does
the SKILL.md example. A hand-written file of negative cases (duplicate
ID, incident from code, cited unsourced, missing and empty citation,
unknown field and tag) gets one error each.

The field list has no `series`. cc/peff-commit-brief adds one; when
that topic is reworked on top of this, the linter's FIELDS needs it.

Citations are matched with nested parentheses and double quotes
skipped, because session quotes can hold a "(" of their own. A quote
with an odd number of double quotes inside it will confuse that;
none of the real briefs has one.
